<Base
  title="Goals"
  description="Collin D. Ching's public goals — written down so they cost something to abandon."
>
  <h1>Goals</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Written goals are commitments. Public goals are expensive to abandon.
    These are mine.
  </p>

  <h2>Do the hard things</h2>
  <p>
    The meta skill: endurance for important-but-painful tasks. Shipping
    publicly. Being seen. Doing the reps that matter even when they're
    uncomfortable. Everything else I want — the learning, the building, the
    business — sits on top of this muscle, so this is the one I'm training
    first.
  </p>

  <h2>Learn, build, and market in public</h2>
  <p>
    The program. Every week: learn something real, build something with it,
    and distribute the work instead of just doing it. Three threads —
    learning AI (plus data science, finance, and whatever else earns my
    curiosity), shipping things built with AI, and learning marketing by
    practicing it in the open.
  </p>

</Base>
